"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:43:34-07:00","id":858337,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/prometheanmilestones/\" target=\"_blank\">There ya go.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T13:56:20-07:00","id":858507,"title":"","content":"Do we know which settings show up in the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:32:53-07:00","id":858531,"title":"","content":"So, Milestones. We got six universal Milestones, thematically linked to alchemical processes, but only <i>projectio</i> has a hard and fast action associated with it. <i>Projectio</i> means drinking from a River of Death, and is also part of the final ritual of the New Dawn (but not exclusive to it). <i>Multiplicatio</i> refers to an act of creation, but can mean the passing of knowledge and experience. <i>Fermentatio</i> seems to about Vitriol, and revolves around its transmutation and capital-T Transmutations. <i>Ceratio</i> means connecting with other Prometheans, and through them, to the world. <i>Separatio</i> is about understanding the gulf between the world and the Promethean. <i>Sublimato</i> involves apprehending the Refinements and their place, and maybe the greater Pilgrimage as a whole. All are revealed through Azothic Memory, except for the Extempore, who have no direct connection to it, perhaps as a result of having no demiurge.<br /> <br /> There are then prescribed Milestones. These are the prizes of Roles and Refinements, which will describe a few examples in the text. Instinctive Milestones are more freeform, descending from the Five Questions asked at character creation (as in the GMC character creation rules, but likely altered for the Created), and are much more personal. No word on whether Extempore have the instinct in question.<br /> <br /> All in all, I don't think they've changed so much as they have been anchored to more concrete character choices and explicitly so. With Roles in the mix, this should work out for Storytellers looking for more guidance in developing Milestones. I think we're still in the dark regarding the larger framework of how the Pilgrimage has evolved, whether it's how the new trait works, how Roles divide of Refinements, or how Vitriol figures in the Beats and Experiences scheme.<br /> <br /> Sidenote: creating a Promethean is no longer a required Milestone, meaning that the balance of Prometheans and Pandorans is no longer as clear. The little creeps probably persist through Firestorms and Centimani rituals and alchemical mishaps, but it seems less likely to happen as risk of the Pilgrimage itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T14:36:18-07:00","id":858532,"title":"","content":"<div c